<%# The closing call to action, shared by the home page and every detail page.

  TWO DESTINATIONS, BOTH REAL. Account creation goes to the application's own registration path, and the
  second action is the published address rendered as a mailto: -- the old page's equivalent band offered a
  trial that cannot start (no plan row exists, and the trial plan id defaults to nil) beside a live-chat
  button that opened nothing (docs/official-website/02-verified-feature-inventory.md section 6).

  THE ONE DARK FIELD ON THE PAGE, and it is full width rather than a rounded slab floating in the margin:
  the band is the page's last word, so it gets the whole measure and the type is set to the same start edge
  as everything above it instead of being centred. Electric blue is readable here and nowhere else -- on
  paper it is 3.3:1 and would fail, on this field it carries the eye to the one live accent.
%>
<section class="mt-20 bg-lyn-ink">
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:flex-row lg:items-end lg:justify-between lg:py-20">
    <div>
      <h2 class="max-w-xl text-balance text-2xl font-semibold leading-[1.4] tracking-tight text-lyn-paper sm:text-3xl">
        <%= t('marketing.cta.title') %>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-base leading-[1.85] text-lyn-paper/70"><%= t('marketing.cta.lede') %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex shrink-0 flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/app/register"
         class="rounded-xl bg-lyn-indigo px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-paper transition-colors hover:bg-lyn-indigo-deep focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue">
        <%= t('marketing.cta.primary') %>
      </a>
      <a href="<%= marketing_support_email_url %>"
         class="rounded-xl border border-lyn-line-dark px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-paper transition-colors hover:border-lyn-blue hover:text-lyn-blue">
        <%= t('marketing.cta.email') %>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
